			},
			"date": "2025-01-24T03:26:27.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> 2024 saw me attend a startling number of funerals for the parents of my friends.  Most were celebrations of the deceased’s life. One in particular contained very little about the person we were there to honour, but it was all about god’s mercy and love and benevolence…. For someone who died in agony from cancer — something I wouldn’t wish on anyone.  </p><p><a href=\"https://mstdn.ca/tags/SelfAwarenessFail\" class=\"mention hashtag\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">#<span>SelfAwarenessFail</span></a></p>",
